      <div type="clause" n="23.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 23.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23.3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>Wealh gafolgelda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.1-4"/> CXX scill., his sunu C<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.2-3"/>, ðeowne LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.3-3"/>, somhwelcne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.4-2"/> fiftegum; Weales hyd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.5-2"/> twelfum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23.3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>Wealh gafolgylda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.1-3"/> CXX scll', his sunu C, þeowne LX, somhwylcne mid fiftig; Weales hyd mid twelfum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23.3" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>Wealh gafolgylda hundtwelftig scill', his sunu hundred<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.1"/>, ðéowne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.2"/> sextig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.3"/> scill', somhwylcne mid fiftig; Weales hyd mid twelfu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="23.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="101" ed="#liebermann"/>ƿealh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.1-2"/> qui gablum reddit hundtwelfti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.2-2"/> scillinga (CXX sol.), filius eius C solid., seruus LX solid. somhƿylcne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.3-2"/> L<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.4"/>; serui corium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.5"/> XII.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="42" ed="#attenborough"/>Wealh gafolgelda CXX scill., his sunu C, ðeowne<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#Ine_23-3.attnote.fn.16"/> LX, somhwelcne fiftegum<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#Ine_23-3.attnote.fn.17"/>; Weales hyd twelfum<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#Ine_23-3.attnote.fn.18"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="23" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="390" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Wealh gafolgelda CXX sciƚƚ, his sunu C, ðeowne LX, somhwelcne fiftegum; Weales hyd twelfum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="101" ed="#liebermann"/>Ein Wälscher<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.de.1"/>, ein Abgabenzahler [hat] 120 Schill. [Wergeld], dessen Sohn 100; einen Hörigen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.de.2"/> [bezahle man] mit 60, manchen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.de.3"/> mit 50; eines [hörigen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.de.4"/>] Wälschen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_23-3.lnote.de.5"/> Haut [die Prügelstrafe kaufe man ab] mit 12 [Schillingen].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">A Welshman, a rent-payer, [has] 120 shillings [wergeld], his son 100; a dependant [is to be paid for] with 60, some with 50; a [dependent] Welshman’s hide [the flogging is to be bought off] with 12 [shillings].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="43" ed="#attenborough"/>[The wergeld of] a Welsh taxpayer [is] 120 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_23-3.attnote.n.1"/>; of his son 100 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_23-3.attnote.n.2"/>. [The amount to be paid for killing] a slave [is normally] 60 [shillings]<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_23-3.attnote.n.3"/>, but in some cases 50 [shillings]<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_23-3.attnote.n.4"/>. A Welshman may compound for a scourging by the payment of 12 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_23-3.attnote.n.5"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="402" ed="#whitelock"/>A Welsh rent-payer<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_23-3.whinote.n.6"/> [has a wergild of] 120 shillings, his son, 100; a slave [is to be paid for with] 60, some with 50; a Welshman's hide with 12 [shillings].<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_23-3.whinote.n.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="391" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>A Welsh tax-payer [has a wergild of] 120 shillings, his son 100, a slave [a worth of] 60, some fifty. A Welshman [can redeem his] skin [from a beating with] twelve [shillings].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="391"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_10">Abt 10–11</ref> <quote>In Æthelberht §16 [L10–11] different ranks of slaves have different worths.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="391"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_32">Ine 32</ref> <quote>§32 sets the wergild of a Welshman who owns no property – that is, a hired worker – at 60 shillings.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="391"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_74">Ine 74</ref> <quote>It is true that §75 requires the owner of a Welsh slave who has killed an Englishman to pay 60 shillings</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="399"><ref target="clause:Ine_32">Ine 32</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="435"><ref target="clause:Ine_74">Ine 74</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="394"><ref target="clause:Northleoda_7">Norðleoda 7–12</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hunder, <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. geänd. in</hi> -dred</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hunder, altered in the 16th cent. to -dred</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. geänd. aus</hi> ðeow</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered in the 16th cent. from ðeow</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ƿealh — scillinga <hi rend="italic">fehlt Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ƿealh — scillinga lacking in Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor Klammer Lond; (eingeklammertes) übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">reading of Lond before the bracket; (the bracketed words) the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ylne <hi rend="italic">R T;</hi> -ilne <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ylne R T; -ilne Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sol. <hi rend="italic">fügt zu M Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sol. added by M Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eorum <hi rend="italic">R;</hi> per <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eorum R; per added by Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gylda hundtwelftig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gylda hundtwelftig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hund, nedþeowne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hund, nedþeowne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sixtig scill. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sixtig scill. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-hwylcne mid f. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-hwylcne mid f. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hyde mid <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hyde mid Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hier bringt</hi> 24,2 <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">here Ld places 24,2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier sollte neues Kapitel beginnen. — Kompositum <hi rend="italic">wealhgafolgelda</hi> nicht anzusetzen! — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Walliser 2; Bauer 1c; Abgabe 8. Auch die <hi rend="italic">Leges inter Brettos</hi> (d. i. Strathclyde) <hi rend="italic">et Scotos,</hi> nach Mitte 12. Jhs., geben Wergelder für König, Graf und Than und dann je für den Sohn; Skene <hi rend="italic">Celtic Scotland</hi> III 218. — Corbett versteht hierunter die unterworfenen Kelten in Somerset und Dorset; <hi rend="italic">Cambridge mediæ. hist.</hi> II 562</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">A new chapter should begin here. — No compound <hi rend="italic">wealhgafolgelda</hi> is to be posited! — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Walliser 2; Bauer 1c; Abgabe 8. The <hi rend="italic">Leges inter Brettos</hi> (i.e. Strathclyde) <hi rend="italic">et Scotos,</hi> after the middle of the 12th cent., likewise give wergilds for king, earl and thane and then for the son of each; Skene <hi rend="italic">Celtic Scotland</hi> III 218. — Corbett understands by this the subjugated Celts in Somerset and Dorset; <hi rend="italic">Cambridge mediæ. hist.</hi> II 562</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ändere: ‘Hörigen nicht Deutscher Abkunft, sondern Walliser Rasse’, da <hi rend="italic">þeowne</hi> Adj., also <hi rend="italic">Wealh</hi> zu ergänzen zwingt, und da auch die folg. Zeile vom Walliser handelt. Der freie Walliser (<hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi> 3a. 8) ohne Land hat ebensoviel Wergeld wie der Walliser Knecht kostet. Verschiedener Wert der Sklaven ist auch sonst bekannt. Die 50 Schilling könnten abgerundet sein von 48, d. i. 1 £, dem sonstigen Sklavenpreis des Unfreien; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7a. b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Alter to: ‘a serf not of German descent, but of Welsh race’, since <hi rend="italic">þeowne</hi> is an adj. and thus requires <hi rend="italic">Wealh</hi> to be supplied, and since the following line too deals with the Welshman. The free Welshman (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 3a. 8) without land has as much wergild as the Welsh slave costs. Differing values of slaves are known elsewhere too. The 50 shillings might be rounded off from 48, i.e. £1, the usual slave-price of the unfree man; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7a. b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q missversteht ein Pronomen als Rechtsterminus</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q misunderstands a pronoun as a legal term</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Prügel 2. 4a. c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Prügel 2. 4a. c</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_23-3.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Unter den Bedeutungen des Worts wählt Q falsch: die Haut des Englischen Knechts galt mehr</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q chooses wrongly among the meanings of the word: the hide of the English slave was worth more</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.attnote.fn.16" n="16" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>ðeowne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">nedþeowne</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.attnote.fn.17" n="17" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>fiftegum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mid fiftig</hi>. H &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>twelfum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mid twelfum</hi>. H &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">185</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">There is perhaps a certain discrepancy, though not an actual contradiction, between this law and cap. 32, which may point to a composite origin (cf. cap. 18, note 1) or to additions having been made after the time of Ine; though this cannot be regarded as certain.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The principle that the head of the household is valued at a greater amount than his son, seems to represent Welsh custom—though the amount of the wergelds here given is far less than those stated in the Welsh laws themselves (cf. Seebohm, <hi rend="italic">Tribal System in Wales</hi>, p. 106). No such principle is to be found in the Anglo-Saxon Laws. Cf. Seebohm, <hi rend="italic">Tribal Custom in A.S. Law</hi>, p. 308.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.attnote.n.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> probably a pound (cf. cap. 59)—the ordinary price of a slave (cf. cap. 3 § 2, 74; IV As. cap. 6 § 6; II Athlr. cap. 5 § 1; <hi rend="italic">Duns.</hi> 7).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.attnote.n.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The context here seems to suggest that slaves in a Welsh community or household are meant.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.attnote.n.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. Ine, cap. 54; Alf. cap. 35.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.whinote.n.6" n="6" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">402</biblScope></bibl><label>rent-payer</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">see</hi> p. 399, n. 4. Apparently the highest class of Welsh peasant is meant.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_23-3.whinote.n.7" n="7" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">402</biblScope></bibl><label>[shillings]</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">i.e. a Welshman must pay this sum to save himself from a flogging.</seg></note>
      </div>
